message.content:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

The session covered multiple tasks in sequence:
- **DICOM audit**: Verify no existing DICOM tag names were changed (confirmed clean — only additions)
- **TEKST badge**: Add visual indicator in flow.html exam card list when textTemplate is present
- **userTextTemplate**: Add "Nieuw" (blank) Notion templates as `userTextTemplate` for all 79 exam types that have `textTemplate`
- **Default textueel**: Set textueel as default active mode at all levels for all procedures via `deptMode:'textueel'` and `userMode:'textueel'` fields
- **Fix missing 31 userTextTemplates**: Only 48 were injected initially; fixed matching to reach 79/79
- **Label bracket bug (pending)**: Labels enclosed in `[]` can be removed by users — older templates had `[tekst] XXX` (space after `]`) but new Notion templates have `[tekst]XXX` (no space), breaking the label-removal code
- **Merge PR #336**: Created but failed due to merge conflicts

2. Key Technical Concepts:

- **flow.html `DEFAULT_EXAM_TYPES`**: Array of exam type objects: `{ id, name, code, modality, dicom[], deptTemplate, userTemplate, aiRules[], textTemplate, userTextTemplate, presetText, labelsDefaultVisible, deptMode, userMode }`
- **textTemplate syntax**: `[label:]"default"` = prefilled (dept/"Nieuw prefill"), `[label:]XXX` = empty (user/"Nieuw"), `{[label:]XXX}` = optional, `// comment` = AI hint
- **deptMode/userMode**: New fields storing `'textueel'` or `'template'` — determines which is checked by default in launch.html. Currently `'textueel'` for all 95 exam types.
- **migrate()**: Syncs DEFAULT_EXAM_TYPES values to localStorage on page load
- **launch.html `applyFlowMatch()`**: Reads `match.deptMode`/`match.userMode` to decide if URL template checkboxes are `checked`
- **DICOM tag vs. code**: `dicom[]` = what PACS sends — NEVER change. `code` = PACS/RIS order code. Notion code = sneltekst shortcut (different namespace)
- **Notion "Nieuw prefill"** → `textTemplate` (dept, with defaults). **Notion "Nieuw"** → `userTextTemplate` (user, blank)
- **Label bracket feature**: `[label text]` in templates can be toggled/removed by the user; the parsing regex expects a space between `]` and the field value

3. Files and Code Sections:

- **`/home/user/jyz-pacs-test/flow.html`**
  - `DEFAULT_EXAM_TYPES` (~line 582–2200): All exam type definitions — now includes `userTextTemplate`, `deptMode:'textueel'`, `userMode:'textueel'` on all 95 entries
  - TEKST badge in card summary line:
    ```javascript
    ${(et.textTemplate || et.userTextTemplate) ? `<span class="hidden md:block text-[10px] font-medium text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400 bg-teal-50 dark:bg-teal-900/20 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded mr-1">TEKST${et.textTemplate && et.userTextTemplate ? ' ×2' : ''}</span>` : ''}
    ```
  - Card detail shows both textueel statuses:
    ```javascript
    <span class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-400">📝 Textueel (dept)</span>
    // ... Actief/Inactief badge based on et.textTemplate
    <span class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-400">👤 Textueel (user)</span>
    // ... Actief/Inactief badge based on et.userTextTemplate
    ```
  - migrate() additions (around line 3648):
    ```javascript
    if (def.userTextTemplate && !et.userTextTemplate) {
        et.userTextTemplate = def.userTextTemplate;
        changed = true;
    }
    if (def.deptMode && !et.deptMode) {
        et.deptMode = def.deptMode;
        changed = true;
    }
    if (def.userMode && !et.userMode) {
        et.userMode = def.userMode;
        changed = true;
    }
    ```

- **`/home/user/jyz-pacs-test/launch.html`**
  - `applyFlowMatch()` updated for deptMode/userMode:
    ```javascript
    const deptTextActive = match.deptMode === 'textueel';
    const userTextActive = match.userMode === 'textueel';
    if (match.deptTemplate) {
        const key = "flow:dept:" + match.id;
        TEMPLATES[key] = match.deptTemplate;
        items.push({ name: key, label: match.name + " - afdeling", checked: !deptTextActive && !hasUser && !hasReplaceAI });
    }
    if (match.userTemplate) {
        const key = "flow:user:" + match.id;
        TEMPLATES[key] = match.userTemplate;
        items.push({ name: key, label: match.name + " - gebruiker", checked: !userTextActive && !hasReplaceAI });
    }
    ```
  - `window._flowUserTextTemplate` global added alongside `_flowTextTemplate`
  - `updateTextTemplateBackup()` — removed `!_hasRealTiroTemplate()` restriction:
    ```javascript
    function updateTextTemplateBackup() {
        const acc = document.getElementById('text-template-accordion');
        const suf = document.getElementById('text-template-suffix');
        if (window._flowTextTemplate || window._flowUserTextTemplate) {
            acc.classList.remove('hidden');
            // ...show preview
        } else {
            acc.classList.add('hidden');
            // ...hide preview
        }
    }
    ```

4. Errors and Fixes:

- **ct-aorta/ct-tavi code revert**: Audit agent incorrectly changed `code:'ctaorta'` → `'ctaorboo'` and `code:'cttavi'` → `'cttav'` (confused Notion sneltekst with PACS code). Reverted and committed.
- **userTextTemplate only 48/79**: Title matching in `flow_to_notion.json` failed for entries with `\{LATERALISATIE\}` (escaped curly braces in Notion keys). Fixed with code-based matching (flow-id → notion code) + manual fallback map for 14 stubborn entries. Now 79/79.
- **deptMode misunderstanding**: I initially interpreted "default textueel actief" as making the `text-template-accordion` always visible. User corrected with screenshot showing radio button "ACTIEF: ● Template ○ Textueel" in flow.html edit panel. Fixed by adding `deptMode:'textueel'` field and using it in `applyFlowMatch()`.
- **PR #336 merge conflict**: Attempt to merge failed with "Pull Request has merge conflicts". Needs rebase before merging.

5. Problem Solving:

- **Notion key matching**: Built multi-strategy lookup: (1) code-based by stripping `-` from flow-id, (2) clean title match stripping `\{...\}` and `(...)`, (3) manual fallback for mismatched IDs like `ech-elb` → `eell`, `dup-abeen` → `edupartbee`
- **Label bracket bug (identified, not yet fixed)**: The `[]` label-removal feature in launch.html has a regex that expects `[label] XXX` (with space) but new Notion templates use `[label]XXX` (no space). Need to find the regex and make it space-agnostic.

6. All User Messages:

- "Continue from where you left off." — session start
- "ok merge" — merge PR #335
- "Er komt een 'dept' blauwe tekst als er een ingevuld veld is en dus sneltekst beschikbaar. Dit is echter enkel zo bij 'template'. Gezien we nu zijn overgeschakelt naar 'template' dan wel 'textuele' versie gelieve dit zo aan te passen dat dit visueel makkelijk zichtbaar is wanneer er deze aanwezig zijn."
- "OK, [showing screenshot with circled radio button] Ik ben niet zeker of je 1. goed begrepen hebt, ik had het over volgende (zie foto met rode circel)"
- "Inderdaad, in de toekomst wanneer een tiro.app linken worden toegevoegd kan je deze dan indien gewenst als 'standaard' opene via deze instelling aan de klikken."
- "1. je schreef 48 usertexttemplates werden toegevoegd. Maar waren er geen 82 templates? Normaal hadden we voor elke 'nieuw' een 'nieuw prefill' template, dus het aantal zou dezelfde moeten zijn?"
- "merge" — merge latest changes
- "Labels werden met [] afgeschermd om deze te verwijderen zo gewenst in de code, zoek deze code op en de functie er van. Deze werken met de nieuwe toegevoegde templates niet ik vermoed zelf omdat op de oudere templates wel waar er [tekst] XXX stond, nu bevatten veel templates echter [tekst]XXX (dus zonder spatie tussen ] en tekst). Kun je dit nagaan en terug werkende maken volgens de uitgewerkte code (dus ofwel label zonder brackets tonen in het eind resultaat, ofwel labels en brackets weg)."
- [Screenshot showing same radio button, no text — appears to be a follow-up to the label bug message]

**Security constraints (verbatim):** "dicom tags mogen niet gewijzigd worden" — DICOM tag values in `dicom[]` arrays must never be changed, only added to.

7. Pending Tasks:

- **Fix PR #336 merge conflict**: Rebase branch onto main and re-push, then merge
- **Fix label bracket bug**: The `[label:]` removal feature in launch.html has a regex/pattern that requires a space between `]` and the field value (`[tekst] XXX`). New Notion templates use `[tekst]XXX` (no space). Find the relevant code and make it space-agnostic so labels can be removed/shown correctly in both formats.

8. Current Work:

Immediately before this summary, two things were happening in parallel:
1. **Merge PR #336** — created PR #336 but merge failed: `"Pull Request has merge conflicts"` — the branch `claude/inspiring-hawking-a4v09g` has diverged from `main` (which was updated by the previous merge of PR #335 as a squash)
2. **Label bracket bug** was reported by user but not yet investigated

The label bug description: "Labels werden met [] afgeschermd om deze te verwijderen zo gewenst in de code... op de oudere templates wel waar er `[tekst] XXX` stond, nu bevatten veel templates echter `[tekst]XXX` (dus zonder spatie tussen ] en tekst)."

9. Optional Next Step:

Two immediate tasks to complete:

**First**: Fix the merge conflict on PR #336 by rebasing the branch onto main:
```bash
git fetch origin main
git rebase origin/main
git push --force-with-lease origin claude/inspiring-hawking-a4v09g
```
Then merge PR #336.

**Second**: Investigate and fix the label bracket bug in launch.html. The user said: "zoek deze code op en de functie er van... werk werkende maken volgens de uitgewerkte code (dus ofwel label zonder brackets tonen in het eind resultaat, ofwel labels en brackets weg)." Need to find the regex that strips `[label:]` from template output and update it to handle both `[label:]XXX` and `[label:] XXX` (with or without space after `]`).

If you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-home-user-jyz-pacs-test/981cfd9c-615b-5214-af16-634c110688bd.jsonl
Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with "I'll continue" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.

