```

And at line 3048: `latestDictationText = text.trim();`

So `sendToDictationFields(text)` calls `setDictationText(text)` which sets `latestDictationText = text`. 

But when `_pipReset()` runs, it clears `_pipDmoTa` by calling `setNativeValue(ta, '')`, which wipes out the textarea in the PiP window. The issue is that the main window's clipboard element captures the dictation text and propagates it through `latestDictationText` and `_pipDmoTa`, but then `_pipReset()` clears everything without properly syncing back to the main window's dictation fields.

